# Which snip-36-prover-backend release strkd bundles into the desktop app.
#
# Single source of truth for the prover version, read by the CI release workflow
# and the staging scripts.
#
# PINNED TO v1.1.3 (RC.6 stack) ON PURPOSE — do not bump blindly:
#   The deployed Starknet Sepolia gateway verifier runs the RC.6 stack and accepts
#   only the "PROOF0" proof envelope. v1.1.3 emits PROOF0 and was confirmed to
#   verify ON-CHAIN (2026-06-16). v1.2.x bumped the sequencer (RC.6 -> ac43943)
#   ahead of the verifier, so it emits "PROOF1" which is REJECTED at admission
#   (node error code 69). Same skew class as the RC.3-vs-RC.6 incident.
#
# Because v1.1.3's PREBUILT binaries bake the build machine's path and can't be
# relocated, the workflow builds v1.1.3 FROM SOURCE via stage-prover-source.sh and
# applies scripts/patch-sequencer-relocatable.py. (stage-prover-prebuilt.sh remains
# for a future verifier that accepts PROOF1 + a relocatable prebuilt release.)
#
# Before bumping: confirm the new version emits a proof the LIVE verifier accepts
# (prove + submit a proof-carrying verify on Sepolia) — see memory
# prover-proof-format-pin and docs/project/status.md.
#
# Releases: https://github.com/starknet-innovation/snip-36-prover-backend/releases
SNIP36_REPO=starknet-innovation/snip-36-prover-backend
SNIP36_RELEASE=v1.1.3
